1
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:04,860
Hi, today, a short video on the "spin".

2
00:00:04,894 --> 00:00:19,326
[Music]

3
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:22,905
My first piece of advice
is to ride a nice spiral,

4
00:00:22,942 --> 00:00:25,852
tightening it bit by bit
until you reach the pivot point.

5
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:28,080
This gives you more momentum.

6
00:00:28,597 --> 00:00:32,308
If you try to turn too early,
you may not have enough momentum

7
00:00:32,332 --> 00:00:34,119
and get thrown outward.

8
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:39,564
Next, stand up straight
and keep your eyes forward,

9
00:00:39,602 --> 00:00:40,602
not on the wheel.

10
00:00:41,113 --> 00:00:43,945
Ride at a good pace,
and above all, smoothly.

11
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:48,620
As you spin, lock the wheel
so you can turn on the spot.

12
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:51,232
Otherwise, it won't turn
and you'll lose your balance.

13
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:56,359
Another very important thing
is to use your arms properly.

14
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:59,752
Start with your arms spread out,
slightly in front of you,

15
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:03,907
and pull them in at the last moment
against your chest or along your body.

16
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:13,092
Avoid jerky movements as you turn,
and don't thrust your hips as you spin.

17
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:15,686
That's harder, and much less pretty.

18
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:21,245
A small exercise to get used to spinning:
ride in a straight line,

19
00:01:21,409 --> 00:01:25,780
and push against a wall or a post
with one arm, while locking the wheel.

20
00:01:27,017 --> 00:01:29,519
There aren't 10,000 ways to do the "spin".

21
00:01:29,624 --> 00:01:31,681
There's no help, no wall to lean on,

22
00:01:32,015 --> 00:01:33,552
you just have to go for it
and keep at it.

23
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:37,226
Ideally on a smooth surface
so the tire slides better.

24
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:42,470
There are plenty of variations
for every level:

25
00:01:42,501 --> 00:01:47,587
several spins in a row,
more turns, riding out backward,

26
00:01:48,231 --> 00:01:52,244
a hop, squeezing your thighs
to take the unicycle with you,

27
00:01:52,575 --> 00:01:54,906
the "one-foot spin", and so on.

28
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,253
Use your imagination.

29
00:01:58,564 --> 00:01:59,564
Good luck.

